<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      A marked block with space-before, which makes FOP's space resolver put a box of its own, with no layout
      manager, at the start of the element list: that box is not the part's content, so the page the marked
      block opens is still the part's (docx4j corpus document 12802). First sequence: a two-column part over
      two pages, then a marked span="all" block with break-before="page". Second: the same with the two-column
      part on one page. Third: a single-column marked block with break-before="page", which opens the part's
      first page (Bf). Fourth: a marked block with space-before reaching the top of page 3 without a break.
    </p>
  </info>
